<!--
  Allen & Heath Xone:K2: a Cadence profile from the online library (A208).

  SOURCE, and only this: the manufacturer's own MIDI documentation.
    XONE:K2 User Guide, Publication AP8509 Issue 3 (Allen & Heath Limited, 2018 (PDF created 2018-10-03)), pages 9 (MIDI Controls), 11 (MIDI Channel Number), 12-13 (Latching Layers), 14-16 (MIDI Implementation Send), 19-20 (MIDI Note Implementation Table)
    https://acueexpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/XoneK2_UG_AP8509_3.pdf
    XONE:K2 User Guide, Publication AP8509 Issue 2 (cross-check only; send chart identical to Issue 3) (Allen & Heath Limited, 2012 (PDF created 2012-08-01)), pages MIDI Implementation Send pages
    https://r2.gear4music.com/media/29/292118/download_292118.pdf
  No mapping file from any other application was read or used.

  status="manual": the message is the manufacturer's. Nobody has tried this map on the hardware
  yet. If a control does nothing, use Learn on that row and tell us at shlabs.contact@gmail.com.
  label="..." is the control's name on the unit, shown in the mapping dialog and the guided tour.

  BEFORE YOU START: Factory settings: global MIDI channel 15, Latching Layers OFF (setup mode option 1).

  CADENCE'S CHOICES:
    Allen & Heath's guide was read from a retailer's unmodified copy of the PDF: allen-heath.com refused automated downloads. The unit's factory MIDI channel is 15, with Latching Layers off.

  LEFT OUT (no Cadence target): Top-row encoder push switches (notes E3 F3 F#3 G3 = 52-55): no Cadence target that fits a push on the filter encoder.; Bottom-row left encoder (CC20, push C#0 = 13): left free.; LAYER button (C0 = 12) and EXIT SETUP button (D#0 = 15): left free.; All amber and green layer messages (CC22-CC69, notes in octaves 4-9): they are sent only when Latching Layers are on.

  A jog wheel that moves too fast or too slow: set its row to Fine, or invert it, in the dialog.
-->
